  "contentHtml": "\n                                    \n                                                                                    <ul>\n                                                                                                                                                    <li><a href=\"/agency/87654367/TNN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">TNN</a></li>\n                                                                                            </ul>\n                                                                                <ul>\n                                                                                            <li>Published On Jul 27, 2026 at 03:42 PM IST</li>\n                                                                                                                                </ul>\n                                    \n                                \n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p>Lucknow: Medical libraries at govt healthcare institutions play a crucial role in improving <a href=\"/tag/health+literacy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">health literacy</a>, combating <a href=\"/tag/medical+misinformation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">medical misinformation</a> and promoting <a href=\"/tag/evidence-based+patient+care\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">evidence-based patient care</a>, a study by researchers from <a href=\"/tag/lucknow+university\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lucknow University</a>’s Department of Library and Information Science has found.The study was conducted across three govt medical institutions in Lucknow — <a href=\"/tag/king+george%e2%80%99s+medical+university\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">King George’s Medical University</a> (KGMU), Sanjay Gandhi Postgraduate Institute of Medical Sciences (<a href=\"/tag/sgpgims\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SGPGIMS</a>) and Dr Ram Manohar Lohia Institute of Medical Sciences (<a href=\"/tag/rmlims\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">RMLIMS</a>).</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>Researchers surveyed 375 participants, including MBBS students, postgraduate medical students, doctors, faculty members and research scholars, to assess the role of medical libraries in healthcare institutions.</p>\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>“The findings showed that digital information resources, e-journals, health literacy programmes and information services offered by medical libraries significantly improved access to reliable medical information,” said LU spokesperson Mukul Srivastava.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>He said a majority of respondents reported that library services helped them distinguish authentic medical information from misinformation, make informed clinical decisions and deliver better-quality patient care.The research, conducted by associate professor <a href=\"/tag/anjali+gulati\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Anjali Gulati</a> and senior research fellow <a href=\"/tag/harman+iftekhar\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Harman Iftekhar</a>, has been published in the internationally reputed Scopus-indexed <a href=\"/tag/journal+of+electronic+resources+in+medical+libraries\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Journal of Electronic Resources in Medical Libraries</a>, published by Routledge, Taylor &amp; Francis Group. The paper was published online on July 19, 2026.                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                    \n\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/87654367/TNN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">TNN</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Jul 27, 2026 at 03:42 PM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Jul 27, 2026 at 03:42 PM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">1 min read</li> -->\n                                </ul>\n                            \n                                        \n\n                    \n\n                    <!-- Comment Section -->\n                                            \n                                        <!-- Comment Section -->\n\n                    \n                      \n    \n            <p>\n                </p><h2>Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. </h2>   \n                <h3>Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights &amp; analysis in your inbox.</h3>\n            <p></p>\n\n            <!-- <figure class=\"top-newsletter-subs__icon-nl\" role=\"presentation\" aria-label=\"Newsletter icon\">\n                <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/icon-newsletter.svg\" alt=\"Newsletter icon\" width=\"55\" height=\"55\">\n            </figure> -->\n        \n            \n                \n                    <h2>All about ETHealthworld industry right on your smartphone! </h2>\n                    <ul>\n                        <li><a href=\"/app\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Download the ETHealthworld App</a> and get the Realtime updates and Save your favourite articles.</li>\n                    </ul>\n     